<BaseLayout title="Flock Safety | Providers | NoRec.US" description="Networked license-plate recognition, vehicle intelligence, video, audio detection, and public-safety software." active="surveillance">
<main class="page_shell provider_detail">
  <header class="article_header provider_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROVIDER / PLATFORM</p>
    <h1>Flock Safety</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Networked license-plate recognition, vehicle intelligence, video, audio detection, and public-safety software.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="provider_scope_notice">
    <span class="status_label">EVIDENCE SCOPE</span>
    <p><strong>Vendor capability</strong> describes the provider’s published product features. <strong>Illinois deployment</strong> is listed only when supported by Illinois records or a clearly labeled secondary source.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS CONNECTION</p>
    <h2>Documented Illinois relationships</h2>
    <div class="provider_evidence_grid">
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Boone County / Belvidere</h3><p>Boone County Sheriff's Office Policy 450 and a City of Belvidere location response document local Flock deployment and policy.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Huntley</h3><p>Huntley's 2023 public-board process approved 17 Flock readers and described vehicle characteristics and a searchable vehicle “fingerprint.”</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>State oversight</h3><p>Illinois Secretary of State audits in 2025 publicly addressed Flock LPR data-sharing compliance.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT / PLATFORM CAPABILITY</p>
    <h2>Published product capabilities</h2>
    <div class="provider_capability_grid">
      <article><h3>Flock LPR</h3><p>Flock describes its LPR system as capturing plate images, vehicle images, plate number/state, vehicle characteristics such as color and make, date/time, and camera location.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Vehicle Signature / FreeForm</h3><p>Flock's current product material advertises searches using vehicle attributes when a complete plate is unavailable.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Connected LPR network</h3><p>Flock markets cross-jurisdiction sharing through an agency-controlled network.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Other platform products</h3><p>The vendor also markets video cameras, mobile trailers, audio detection, drones, FlockOS, Flock911 and related software. Their existence does not establish Illinois deployment.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / GOVERNANCE QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2>Privacy and governance</h2>
    <div class="provider_questions">
      <details><summary>Retention</summary><p>Flock's June 2026 LPR policy says default LPR retention is seven days, but its August 2026 Evidence Policy describes a standard 30-day customer-data retention period unless otherwise specified. Customer contracts/policies therefore matter.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Sharing</summary><p>Flock says customers choose whether to share LPR data with other customers, subject to law and policy.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Auditability</summary><p>Flock advertises per-search audit logs and customer-controlled access.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Facial recognition</summary><p>Flock's current LPR product page states facial recognition is not included and not planned for that LPR product.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS JURISDICTION FILES</p>
